<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46091" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sub-sto</span></b> , āre, v. n.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To stand</i> or <i>be under</i> or
				<i>among</i>, <i>to be present</i>
			(very rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not in Cic.): si pure substante non rumpuntur
					hi tumores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					6, 10 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nullo dolore substante,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2, 7
						<i>med.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 12,
			2</span></i>.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To stand firm</i>, <i>hold out</i>, =
			subsisto: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">metuo, ut substet hospes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 5, 4, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>